Appendix H — Value of Epistemic Reduction: Formal Properties

H.1 Proposition H.1 (Non-negativity)

Statement. For any investigation operator \mathcal{I}_e with \mathcal{I}_e(\Theta_{\mathrm{param}}) \subseteq \Theta_{\mathrm{param}} and any policy (\pi,\tau),

\mathrm{VOR}_e(\pi,\tau) = \sup_{\theta \in \Theta_{\mathrm{param}}} P_\theta(B_r) - \sup_{\theta \in \mathcal{I}_e(\Theta_{\mathrm{param}})} P_\theta(B_r) \geq 0.

Proof. Since \mathcal{I}_e(\Theta_{\mathrm{param}}) \subseteq \Theta_{\mathrm{param}}, the supremum over a subset is at most the supremum over the full set. The difference is therefore non-negative. ∎

H.2 Proposition H.2 (Zero characterization)

Statement. \mathrm{VOR}_e(\pi,\tau) = 0 if and only if the supremum of P_\theta(B_r) over \Theta_{\mathrm{param}} is attained in \mathcal{I}_e(\Theta_{\mathrm{param}}) (or is approached arbitrarily closely by elements of \mathcal{I}_e).

Proof. (\Leftarrow): if the supremum is attained in \mathcal{I}_e, the two suprema are equal. (\Rightarrow): if the two suprema are equal and \mathcal{I}_e \subseteq \Theta_{\mathrm{param}}, then the full-set supremum is also the subset supremum, which means the maximum is attained (or approached) within \mathcal{I}_e. ∎

H.3 Corollary H.3 (Additivity for nested investigations)

Statement. For nested investigations \mathcal{I}_{e_2} \subseteq \mathcal{I}_{e_1} \subseteq \Theta_{\mathrm{param}},

\mathrm{VOR}_{e_2} = \mathrm{VOR}_{e_1} + \left[ \sup_{\theta \in \mathcal{I}_{e_1}} P_\theta(B_r) - \sup_{\theta \in \mathcal{I}_{e_2}} P_\theta(B_r) \right].

Proof. Telescoping sum. ∎

Remark H.1. Corollary H.3 provides an operational decomposition: the total value of an investigation sequence is the sum of the marginal values of each successive investigation. This supports the pre-posterior analysis: to compare candidate investigations, compare their marginal VOR contributions at the current uncertainty set.

