K.4 Open boundary problems

The following are identified as open issues in the mechanism-indexed classification:

1. Multi-element missions. Flight 7 shows that the single-trajectory framework of TARA v0.3 is insufficient for integrated missions. Extension to \mathcal{W} = \mathcal{W}_{\mathrm{booster}} \times \mathcal{W}_{\mathrm{ship}} with cross-element hazard dependencies is required.
2. Mechanism co-dominance. Some trajectories activate multiple mechanisms simultaneously (e.g., fire plus structural collapse). The set-valued \tilde{\mu} handles this by assigning multiple mechanisms; the ambiguity interval (C.3) reports the resulting uncertainty.
3. Delayed mechanisms. Thermal degradation (e.g., through-tile heating) may manifest hours after capture, outside typical \Delta. The horizon-truncation flag (Appendix G) is designed to detect this, but cannot resolve it.
4. Regulatory mapping. The E_c criterion of 14 CFR 450.101 aggregates collective risk across all receptors. TARA's receptor-specific constraints are conceptually aligned but not identical to E_c. A full mapping is required before TARA can be proposed as a regulatory decision tool.

